1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:04,840
In Map Visualizations, start on
Library and search for Calls by type.

2
00:00:05,369 --> 00:00:08,819
Read the matching template
description: it shows recent calls

3
00:00:08,819 --> 00:00:10,710
as dots coloured by call type.

4
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:13,829
Select that result, then open Customize.

5
00:00:14,239 --> 00:00:18,450
The heading changes from the earlier
Call hot zones view to Calls by type.

6
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:21,870
Choosing a template gives you a
starting configuration that you can

7
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:24,040
inspect before saving your own view.

8
00:00:24,269 --> 00:00:28,529
Under When, this template has Date
range set to Last ninety days.

9
00:00:28,950 --> 00:00:31,779
Days of the week and Hours of
the day are shown below it.

10
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:36,279
The page explains that leaving those
buttons unselected includes every day

11
00:00:36,309 --> 00:00:38,580
and hour, using the department time zone.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,010
Keep this time scope for the exercise.

13
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:45,119
Check these controls whenever you
compare demand, because a different time

14
00:00:45,119 --> 00:00:47,010
window answers a different question.

15
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:51,049
Scroll within Customize to
Which calls and open Call types.

16
00:00:51,439 --> 00:00:55,880
The unfiltered view shows seventeen calls
and eighty-two percent with a location.

17
00:00:56,370 --> 00:00:59,050
Check Investigation,
then close the selector.

18
00:00:59,429 --> 00:01:03,880
Its button now reads Investigation, and
the result changes to eight calls with

19
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:05,829
sixty-three percent having a location.

20
00:01:06,249 --> 00:01:09,759
This shows the effect of the selected
filter on the same time window.

21
00:01:10,159 --> 00:01:13,359
The other visible selectors
remain All in this exercise.

22
00:01:13,499 --> 00:01:16,019
Compare the filtered
summary with the map legend.

23
00:01:16,469 --> 00:01:19,760
Eight calls match the filter,
while the Investigation legend

24
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,799
contains five located entries.

25
00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:25,950
The summary rounds that location
completeness to sixty-three percent.

26
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:30,989
A map shows where located activity
appears; its dots do not account for

27
00:01:30,989 --> 00:01:33,140
calls that lack a usable location.

28
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:36,679
Check this measure before
treating a sparse map as evidence

29
00:01:36,679 --> 00:01:37,950
that little work occurred.

30
00:01:38,419 --> 00:01:41,380
These numbers describe the
fictional recorded dataset.

31
00:01:41,639 --> 00:01:44,540
In Layers, review the enabled Calls layer.

32
00:01:44,899 --> 00:01:49,360
Data is Calls, described as one
point per call at the call location.

33
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:55,039
Show as is Dots, Color by is
Call type, and Value is Count.

34
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:59,550
Opacity and Dot size are separate
display controls below these choices.

35
00:01:59,899 --> 00:02:01,729
Keep the shown configuration here.

36
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:05,829
Reading the data source and display
choices together helps you explain

37
00:02:05,829 --> 00:02:09,550
what the symbols represent, rather
than judging only their appearance.

38
00:02:09,719 --> 00:02:11,099
Select Save as new.

39
00:02:11,749 --> 00:02:16,129
In Save as a new visualization,
enter the fictional name shown here

40
00:02:16,359 --> 00:02:20,440
and a Description that records the
purpose, date scope and filter.

41
00:02:20,879 --> 00:02:24,690
Leave Share with the whole department
unchecked for this private exercise.

42
00:02:24,959 --> 00:02:29,190
The choice is visible beside the form,
so check it deliberately before saving.

43
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:32,110
This walkthrough saves a
view for the current user.

44
00:02:32,419 --> 00:02:33,409
Select Save.

45
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:36,750
Open Library and check
Saved visualizations.

46
00:02:37,179 --> 00:02:41,440
Under My visualizations, the
named Investigation demand review

47
00:02:41,469 --> 00:02:45,070
appears with its description
and Only visible to you label.

48
00:02:45,429 --> 00:02:47,829
The same saved name is
now the page heading.

49
00:02:48,259 --> 00:02:51,130
These are returned application
results after the save,

50
00:02:51,319 --> 00:02:52,860
rather than the unsaved form.

51
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:57,440
Confirm the intended entry and visibility
label before using the view again.

52
00:02:57,759 --> 00:03:01,989
Open the saved visualization in a
fresh page and return to Customize.

53
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,149
Date range still reads Last ninety days.

54
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:09,339
Scroll to Call types and check
that Investigation is retained.

55
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:15,470
Then inspect the layer again: Calls,
Dots, Call type and Count remain selected.

56
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:19,569
This reopening check verifies
the stored configuration beyond

57
00:03:19,569 --> 00:03:20,930
the form where it was prepared.

58
00:03:21,339 --> 00:03:24,739
It does not depend on remembering
the settings from the earlier screen.

59
00:03:24,909 --> 00:03:29,610
With the side panel closed, read the saved
map and Investigation legend together.

60
00:03:30,019 --> 00:03:33,669
Scroll below it to see the eight-call
total, location percentage,

61
00:03:33,959 --> 00:03:37,760
When calls come in grid, and
Most common call types summary.

62
00:03:38,230 --> 00:03:41,060
The latter still shows
Investigation and eight.

63
00:03:41,619 --> 00:03:45,459
Response-time cards contain dashes
in this view, and the page explains

64
00:03:45,459 --> 00:03:47,240
their data and layer requirements.

65
00:03:47,689 --> 00:03:50,560
A dash is not a measured
zero-minute response.

66
00:03:50,859 --> 00:03:54,529
Use the displayed results for the
question this view actually answers.

67
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:58,790
The same process can support community
paramedicine and mental health response

68
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:03,929
planning, search-and-rescue activity
reviews, security service demand, wildland

69
00:04:03,929 --> 00:04:09,539
contractor workload, industrial emergency
response, and fire and E M S departments.

70
00:04:09,999 --> 00:04:13,750
Choose the permitted call types and
time scope relevant to your team.

71
00:04:14,199 --> 00:04:18,699
Inspect the display settings, check
location completeness, save the intended

72
00:04:18,699 --> 00:04:20,930
visibility, and reopen the result.

73
00:04:21,439 --> 00:04:24,310
A useful planning view is
one whose filters and data

74
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:25,930
limitations you can explain.



